<title>USB specifications</title>
<body>
<p>Depending on the model, some USB connectors might not be available
on your computer.</p>
<section><table colsep="1" pgwide="1" rowsep="1">
<tgroup cols="2"><colspec colname="col1" colwidth="39.20%"/><colspec colname="col2" colwidth="60.80%"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry colsep="0" valign="middle"><?PubTbl cell border-left-style="none"?>Connector
name</entry>
<entry valign="middle"><?PubTbl cell border-right-style="none"?>Description</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry colsep="0" valign="middle"><?PubTbl cell border-left-style="none"?><p><image href="usb.jpg" placement="break" scope="local">
<alt>USB-A connectors</alt></image><ul>
<li><p><image href="a_tp_usbicon1-02.jpg" scope="local"><alt> USB-A connector (Hi-Speed USB)</alt></image> USB-A
connector (Hi-Speed USB)</p></li>
<li><p><image href="a_tp_usbicon1-03.jpg" scope="local"><alt> USB-A connector (USB 10Gbps)</alt></image> USB-A
connector (USB 10Gbps)</p></li>
</ul></p></entry>
<entry valign="middle"><?PubTbl cell border-right-style="none"?><ul>
<li><p>Connect USB-A compatible devices, such as a USB-A keyboard,
USB-A mouse, USB-A storage device, or USB-A printer.</p></li>
<li><p>Charge USB-A compatible devices with a maximum output voltage
and current of:<ul>
<li><p>USB-A connector (Hi-Speed USB): 5 V, 0.9 A</p></li>
<li><p>USB-A connector (USB 10Gbps): 5 V, 3 A</p></li>
</ul></p></li>
</ul></entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry colsep="0" valign="middle"><?PubTbl cell border-left-style="none"?><p><image href="usb_c.jpg" placement="break" scope="local"><alt>USB-C connectors</alt></image><ul>
<li><p><image href="a_tp_usbicon1-03.jpg" scope="local"><alt> USB-C connector (USB 10Gbps)</alt></image> USB-C
connector (USB 10Gbps)</p></li>
<li><p><image href="a_tp_usbicon_05.jpg" scope="local"><alt> USB-C connector (USB 20Gbps)</alt></image> USB-C
connector (USB 20Gbps)</p></li>
<li><p><image href="usb4_icon_2.jpg" scope="local"><alt>USB-C connector (USB4 40Gbps) icon</alt></image> USB-C connector (USB4 40Gbps)</p></li>
</ul></p></entry>
<entry valign="middle"><?PubTbl cell border-right-style="none"?><ul>
<!--Confirm with DEV whether all the following functions are supported.-->
<li><p>Charge USB-C compatible devices with a maximum output voltage
and current of 5 V and 3 A.</p></li>
<li><p>Connect to USB-C accessories to help expand your computer functionality.
To purchase USB-C accessories, go to <xref format="html" href="https://www.lenovo.com/accessories" scope="external">https://www.lenovo.com/accessories</xref>.</p></li>
<li><p>The USB-C connector (USB4 40Gbps) can additionally connect
to an 8K display and charge a compatible device when the computer
is off, in sleep, or hibernation.<note>Maximum display resolution
depends on the display, connected graphics card, and cable.</note></p></li>
</ul></entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table><note>Only the USB-C connectors (USB4 40Gbps) in the PCIe
card area support display connection. Do not use any other USB-C connectors
for displays.</note></section>
